---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import SpecificationWorkbench from "../components/SpecificationWorkbench.astro";
import AudienceNavigator from "../components/AudienceNavigator.astro";
import ThirdSpacePortal from "../components/ThirdSpacePortal.astro";
import PublicArchiveSwitchboard from "../components/PublicArchiveSwitchboard.astro";
---
<Base
  wide
  pageClass="instrument-home"
  image="/people/ian-editorial.webp"
  description="Ian Helfrich is a research economist and award-winning educator offering quantitative instruction, research mentorship, and custom training from high school through professional practice."
>
  <SpecificationWorkbench />

  <section class="ih-evidence" aria-label="Selected evidence">
    <div><strong>1,200+</strong><span>recent-year teaching hours</span></div>
    <div><strong>450+</strong><span>students across classrooms and private practice</span></div>
    <div><strong>5.0</strong><span>average across 175+ public ratings</span></div>
    <div><strong>2023</strong><span>Georgia Tech Graduate TA of the Year</span></div>
  </section>

  <AudienceNavigator />

  <section class="ih-practice" aria-labelledby="practice-title">
    <header class="ih-section-intro">
      <div>
        <span class="ih-section-number">02 / THE PRACTICE</span>
        <h2 id="practice-title">Show me where<br />the reasoning breaks.</h2>
      </div>
      <p>
        Sometimes the fix is one missing idea. Sometimes a student needs a semester of connected work. Sometimes a research design has to be taken apart before it can be trusted. I scope those problems differently.
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="ih-service-ledger">
      <article>
        <span class="ih-ledger-index">01</span>
        <div>
          <span class="ih-ledger-type">PRIVATE INSTRUCTION</span>
          <h3>Find the missing model</h3>
        </div>
        <p>A wrong answer is often the last visible link in a longer chain. We find the first weak link, rebuild it, and test whether the idea survives a new problem.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>High school · undergraduate · MBA · graduate</li>
          <li>SAT/ACT · AP · R · Stata · Python · Excel</li>
        </ul>
        <a href="/work-with-me#private">View format →</a>
      </article>

      <article>
        <span class="ih-ledger-index">02</span>
        <div>
          <span class="ih-ledger-type">RESEARCH MENTORSHIP</span>
          <h3>Make the design answer the question</h3>
        </div>
        <p>We state the object, decide what comparison could identify it, inspect the code, and keep the final claim inside what the evidence can carry.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Independent projects · theses · dissertations · papers</li>
          <li>Design review · code review · defense preparation</li>
        </ul>
        <a href="/work-with-me#research">View format →</a>
      </article>

      <article>
        <span class="ih-ledger-index">03</span>
        <div>
          <span class="ih-ledger-type">TEAMS + INSTITUTIONS</span>
          <h3>Put the team’s real problem on screen</h3>
        </div>
        <p>I build the training around the models, data, and decisions already on the team’s desk. The examples and diagnostics stay with the group after I leave.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Workshops · cohorts · curriculum architecture</li>
          <li>Econometrics · causal inference · data workflows</li>
        </ul>
        <a href="/work-with-me#institutions">View format →</a>
      </article>
    </div>

    <div class="ih-practice-close">
      <p><strong>Your judgment is the deliverable.</strong> I teach, question, demonstrate, review, and debug alongside you. I do not take exams, fabricate analysis, or ghostwrite work.</p>
      <a class="ih-action" href="/work-with-me">See fit, formats, and rates</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <ThirdSpacePortal />

  <PublicArchiveSwitchboard />

  <section class="ih-profile" aria-labelledby="profile-title">
    <figure class="ih-profile-image">
      <img src="/people/ian-editorial.webp" alt="Ian Helfrich" width="400" height="400" loading="lazy" />
      <figcaption>IAN T. S. HELFRICH · ECONOMIST / EDUCATOR</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <div class="ih-profile-copy">
      <span class="ih-section-number">05 / THE PERSON IN THE ROOM</span>
      <h2 id="profile-title">A research economist<br />who builds the instruments.</h2>
      <p class="ih-profile-lead">
        I am a Georgia Tech-trained economist, quantitative researcher, and award-winning educator. I work across econometrics, labor, trade, networks, spatial analysis, and the harder question underneath all of them: how did this number become evidence?
      </p>
      <div class="ih-profile-notes">
        <p><span>RESEARCH</span>AI and labor · trade and networks · place-based policy · spatial econometrics</p>
        <p><span>TEACHING</span>SAT and AP foundations · undergraduate and MBA coursework · graduate methods · professional training</p>
        <p><span>TOOLS</span>R · Stata · Python · Julia · GIS · reproducible research systems</p>
      </div>
      <div class="ih-profile-links">
        <a href="/about">Read the full background →</a>
        <a href="/cv">Open CV →</a>
      </div>
    </div>
    <blockquote>
      “The best session ends when you can find the next mistake before I do.”
    </blockquote>
  </section>

  <section class="ih-inquiry" aria-labelledby="inquiry-title">
    <span class="ih-section-number">06 / START WITH THE REAL PROBLEM</span>
    <h2 id="inquiry-title">Where does the<br />reasoning break?</h2>
    <p>Send the problem, what you have tried, and the actual deadline. I will tell you whether I can help, what the smallest useful engagement is, and what it costs.</p>
    <div>
      <a class="ih-action ih-action--light" href="/work-with-me#inquiry">Start an inquiry</a>
      <a href="mailto:ianthelfrich@gmail.com">ianthelfrich@gmail.com</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
